WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.150
Film Courage: Let’s talk about this hypothetical
class of 20 people, 2 excellent students that

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:07.850
you think have potential to have careers and
the 18 that don’t.

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:12.579
Do you think those 18 people want to hear
the truth?

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:19.279
Know that they can be better, it’s malleable,
you can mold them to write better but do they

00:00:19.279 --> 00:00:20.279
really want to hear it?

00:00:20.279 --> 00:00:24.020
We talk about this growth mindset versus whatever
the other side of that coin might be.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.140
Corey Mandell: The fixed mindset.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:26.269
Film Courage: Okay.

00:00:26.269 --> 00:00:31.990
So how do you know you’re experiencing a
student with the fixed-mindset and they don’t

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:32.990
want to hear it?

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:34.950
Corey Mandell: Perfect, perfect, perfect question.

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:36.739
That is such a smart question.

00:00:36.739 --> 00:00:45.109
So the fixed-mindset first of all believes
that if you want to be a writer you either

00:00:45.109 --> 00:00:47.390
have this talent or you don’t.

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:52.309
So then you are constantly have this voice
in your head that says ‘Do I have what it

00:00:52.309 --> 00:00:53.309
takes?

00:00:53.309 --> 00:00:54.309
Do I have the talent?

00:00:54.309 --> 00:00:55.379
Am I wasting my time?

00:00:55.379 --> 00:00:58.629
Am I going to get a career or is it never
going to happen for me?’

00:00:58.629 --> 00:01:04.730
That constant fear-based chatter is that fixed-mindset.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:11.460
And because of that the fixed mindset (and
you asked such a smart question) it desires

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:12.460
an outcome.

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:16.700
So if I have a script and I go “Hey, will
you guys read my script and just give me your

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:17.700
feed back.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:20.040
I want to know what you think?”

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:22.310
There is the fixed mindset and the growth
mindset and they’re both there.

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:23.650
I don’t think it’s one or another.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.680
They both exist, it’s just sort of a ratio.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:29.570
Are you 90 percent growth mindset and 10-percent
fixed?

00:01:29.570 --> 00:01:33.729
When I give you guys a script and say “Tell
me what you think,” my fixed-mindset wants

00:01:33.729 --> 00:01:34.750
an outcome.

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:38.689
It wants you two to say “Well, now I know
why you had a career.

00:01:38.689 --> 00:01:40.060
Now I know why you teach others.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:42.340
This may be the best script I’ve ever read.

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:45.810
I’m literally in awe to be in the same room
with you.

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:49.210
I didn’t know a human being could write
this well?

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:51.040
This is the most amazing script ever!”

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:54.270
Like that’s what my fixed mindset wants
to hear.

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:58.380
And when it doesn’t hear it, it’s going
to throw a temper tantrum.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:01.780
And at that point it has two choices and only
two choices.

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:06.880
Which is “What’s wrong with you guys?”
or “What’s wrong with me?”

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:11.160
So you always hear writers out there say “Yeah,
my manager said that the characters weren't

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:12.360
strong enough.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:13.740
You know, I’ve got to change managers.

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:16.250
I mean, he doesn’t know what he’s talking
about.”

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:19.410
or they’ll say “Yeah, my manager said
that the characters weren’t good enough.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:22.890
I don’t know…I don’t know why I’m
no good at characters?”

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:26.600
There is something wrong with you or there
is something wrong with me.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:29.870
It’s the only choices that it has.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:34.650
The growth mindset does not crave or desire
an outcome.

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:37.110
It desires the truth.

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:41.240
So the growth mindset wants to know what did
you honestly think and why did you think it?

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:45.720
Let’s say that there are part of my script
that you really loved and there was a section

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:50.240
of the script that you just didn’t care
for.

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:51.240
Why?

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:52.530
And not in a defensive way.

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:54.240
And not in an attacking way.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.240
But why?

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:56.240
Because it’s like a detective.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:58.080
It’s like “Hhmmm?

00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:59.620
What plays in my head is amazing.

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:00.960
It’s not amazing for you.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:01.960
I want to know why.

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:03.410
Where is that disconnect.”

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:07.950
Maybe there is a piece of information, a context,
that I knew that you didn’t.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:10.150
I didn’t get out well enough.

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:14.530
And if I could just rewrite it so that becomes
more viscerally clear to people, maybe you’ll

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:16.290
then have the experience I want.

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:21.370
Maybe that section I like it for very personal
reasons but it actually disconnects from this…there

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:22.590
are a whole million reasons.

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:30.980
But if I…and maybe…the reason you didn’t
love my script, the honest truth is, the characters

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:33.220
just weren’t compelling enough for you.

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:34.220
They fell kind of flat.

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:38.170
They felt like they kind of all spoke the
same way.

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:41.480
That’s not now a rewrite (which is the mistake
most people make).

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:49.440
That is ‘Okay, I’m not yet strong enough
at characters…the story…the characters

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:54.320
are great but it kind of wandered around and
it just didn’t seem like it had a forward

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:59.380
thrust and maybe I’m just not good at that
forward thrust.

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:00.380
Great!

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:03.090
The fixed-mindset (of course) is freaking
out.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:07.620
But the growth-mindset is celebrating because
it’s like ‘Okay, now I know what I can

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:09.240
do moving forward to get better as a writer.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:14.020
and I’ve got to figure out how do I train
myself to get better at forward thrust or

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.660
better at characters.’

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:23.101
And so if you follow a growth mindset (when
you get feedback) if you love my script from

00:04:23.101 --> 00:04:24.750
top to bottom.

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:29.560
And I know the process that I use to create
it and I can replicate that process, that

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:31.090
is great news for me.

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:35.680
If you didn’t love my script, top to bottom
and I can talk to you in the right way to

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:41.820
figure out why you didn’t, where the disconnects
were and I could realize where I have a weakness.

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:43.750
Where I need to get better at a skill set.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:47.690
Where I need to create a new talent or get
better at a talent and I can figure out how

00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:50.500
to do it, that’s amazing.

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:55.750
So the growth mindset is not looking for an
outcome, it’s looking for the truth.

00:04:55.750 --> 00:05:01.190
So your question was really profound, those
18 people, did they want to know that they

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:03.030
are the 18 people?

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:06.900
If you ask them, they will all say yes.

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:12.880
The reality is, if you were to tell them (and
I never did).

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:15.440
For right or wrong reasons, that was a line
I never crossed.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:20.590
I would never tell someone if I thought they
had what it took or I didn’t.

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:23.410
Because I felt like that is just my opinion.

00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:25.190
What is my opinion worth at the end of the
day?

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:28.190
And I don’t want to inflict that on someone,
positively or negatively.

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:29.680
So, I don’t know.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:37.280
I’m not saying this was the right decision
but as a teacher (to this day) if someone

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:39.710
says ‘Do you think I have what it takes
or not…well first of all, I’ll say go

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:42.210
read the book MINDSET [by author and Stanford
University psychologist Carol S. Dweck, Ph.D.]

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:43.210
because that is a fixed-mindset question.

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:49.950
But even if I actually have an opinion, I’ll
never tell someone.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:57.870
But if someone were to tell those people and
they would say “I want to know the truth.”

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:02.060
and that is true for their growth mindset
but their fixed mindset does not want to know

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:03.400
the truth, it wants an answer.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:06.590
It wants a specific answer, it wants a yes.

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:10.480
Or the fixed mindset would be okay with “I
don’t think you have what it takes but I

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:13.620
don’t think it will take that long for you
to get there.”

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:15.280
The fixed mindset is like “Aaahhh!

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:16.670
All right.

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:18.370
I’ll settle for that.”

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:21.620
But anything beyond that and then the fixed
mindset is like “Well, what do you know?”

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:24.000
or “Yeah, I don’t know?”

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:31.050
So the reality is what I’ve learned is we’re
always both fixed mindset and growth mindset

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:35.440
and if you really do the work, you can feel
the ratios.

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:40.400
And in fact people often ask me why I teach
and there’s a lot of answers.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:47.830
But I’ll tell you one of the main reasons
that I do this is as a writer I had a very

00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:50.040
unhealthy relationship with my writing.

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:57.410
It was really a tortuous experience because
as a writer I was about as fixed mindset as

00:06:57.410 --> 00:06:59.710
you could be.

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:02.830
As a teacher, I’m about as growth mindset
as you can be.

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:10.050
So for some reason, teaching is one space
in my life where it is just so easy to be

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:12.340
egoless and growth mindset.

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:18.750
And for other people, maybe that is religion
or parenting or whatever.

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:19.820
For me, it’s teaching.

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:21.760
Not sure why, but it is.

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:23.580
And I didn’t even know about mindset at
the time.

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:25.590
It was something I learned later on.

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:28.260
A brilliant student said ‘Hey, you should
read this book.

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:29.260
I think you’d like it.”

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:30.260
And I was like ‘Oh, my Gosh.

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:31.920
Where has this been my whole life?’

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:39.139
And so for me, writing had all these demons
and anxiety and fears.

00:07:39.139 --> 00:07:43.580
And it was just this…I was a very angry
person.

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:50.540
And it was either ‘What the F is wrong with
my agent or this executive and not what was

00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:57.140
wrong with me and those were my only two choices
(and as a teacher) it allows me to live in

00:07:57.140 --> 00:08:03.580
a growth mindset place and it’s very healing
for me and I get so much out of that.

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:09.530
And I really love working with writers and
helping them find and stay in that growth

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:12.630
mindset because that is so important to a
writer.

